  "notes": "West leads the ♥K against 4♠. After the defense takes the first 3 heart tricks and switches to clubs, South must win the ♣A and take the rest of the tricks. South will have to find a way to dispose of his 2 club losers.\n\nDummy's diamonds are the only possible source of extra tricks.\n\nSouth crosses to dummy in trump and leads a diamond. If East covers with the ♦A South can ruff and later use dummy's 2 remaining diamonds for club discards. There are plenty of trump entries to reach the diamond winners in dummy.\n\nIf East plays low on the first round of diamonds, South discards a club. When West cannot win this trick, another diamond is played from dummy for a second ruffing finesse. As long as East has the ♦A, he is powerless to defeat the contract. If West was dealt the ♦A, South can never make the contract.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♥K against 4♠. After the defense takes the first 3 heart tricks and switches to clubs, South must win the ♣A and take the rest of the tricks. South will have to find a way to dispose of his 2 club losers.",
    "Dummy's diamonds are the only possible source of extra tricks.",
    "South crosses to dummy in trump and leads a diamond. If East covers with the ♦A South can ruff and later use dummy's 2 remaining diamonds for club discards. There are plenty of trump entries to reach the diamond winners in dummy.",
    "If East plays low on the first round of diamonds, South discards a club. When West cannot win this trick, another diamond is played from dummy for a second ruffing finesse. As long as East has the ♦A, he is powerless to defeat the contract. If West was dealt the ♦A, South can never make the contract."
  ],
